  "title": "Training datasets for epilepsy analysis: sliding-window features derived from the Freiburg intracranial EEG database (Riccio et al. 2024), processed-data release",
  "description": "This derivative dataset redistributes 20 per-patient feature tables computed from the Freiburg intracranial EEG database. Each row is a 2-second sliding window (1-second step) with 1080 univariate and bivariate features across six frequency bands and six electrodes. Windows are labelled by seizure phase (pre-ictal, ictal, post-ictal, inter-ictal), which makes the tables suitable for training machine-learning models for epileptic seizure analysis. No raw recordings are included.",
  "methods_description": "Six intracranial EEG electrodes per patient (three in the epileptic focus, three outside it) were band-pass filtered into six bands (alpha, beta1, beta2, low gamma, medium gamma, high gamma). Fourteen univariate and eight bivariate features were computed per electrode and band in 2 s windows with a 1 s step, using the authors' Training Builder tool. The source CSV files were copied byte-for-byte from Zenodo and verified by md5 checksum.",
